From 9c35e784b6b6a0475ac6eec4b59c58b90725d84c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: adesh chaudhari <superbhel7@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 7 Aug 2026 08:29:46 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 9/9] feat(frontend): auth-aware navigation, profile and
 guarded routes
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Ties the session into the chrome and closes the last of the static content.

- HeaderNavbar reflects the real session: Sign in when signed out, a profile
  menu when signed in, and the Admin link only for ROLE_ADMIN. Its city picker
  is derived from the live event feed rather than a hardcoded three (YG-7).
- App.jsx puts every JWT-only page behind ProtectedRoute and the whole /admin
  subtree behind AdminRoute. /admin/login stays outside it — it is the way in.
- ProfilePage drops avatar, memberSince and preferred city for good; no such
  columns exist. It renders what the JWT gives us and states plainly that
  phone/email need GET /api/users/me (SZ-4). The edit form is gone rather than
  pretending to save against an endpoint that does not exist (YG-12).
- FooterSection listed six categories, three of which (Sports, Workshops,
  Theatre) never existed in the API. It now renders the backend's four and
  deep-links each into the events listing. The dead href='#' links and the
  newsletter box are gone — nothing was behind either.
- EventsListingPage now syncs its filters from the query string on change, not
  only on mount, so a category link clicked while already on /events applies.
